-- ---------- advanced (15 questions) ----------
insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000000', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'Under Amendment 1, what condition must be established by the risk management process before a software item may be classified as Class A?', '["The software item has no user interface", "The risk management process determines the software item cannot contribute to a hazardous situation", "The software item runs on Class I medical hardware only", "The software item was developed before the current regulatory framework applied"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Amendment 1 revised §4.3 a) so that Class A must be established by the risk management process, not assumed from functionality. Note there are two routes to Class A, and this is the first: either the software system cannot contribute to a hazardous situation at all, or it can but the resulting risk is not unacceptable once risk control measures external to the software have been considered. Either way the determination has to come out of the risk analysis — it cannot be inferred from the software looking harmless.', 0)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000001', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'Under Amendment 1, a software item is the only measure controlling a risk of serious injury or death. Which safety class must it be assigned?', '["Class A", "Class B", "Class C", "The class is determined by the hardware platform it runs on"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Class C — but the citation catches people out. Amendment 1 marked §4.3 b) as ''Not used'' and moved this requirement into §7.2.2 b), which requires a software item contributing to the implementation of a risk control measure to be assigned a safety class based on the risk that the measure is controlling, referring back to §4.3 a). Under §4.3 a) as amended, the class is C where unacceptable risk remains after risk controls external to the software and the possible harm is death or serious injury — which is the position when the software is the only thing controlling that risk.', 1)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000002', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'Amendment 1 introduced a clarified distinction between two key terms. Which pairing is correct?', '["HAZARD = the circumstances of exposure; HAZARDOUS SITUATION = the potential source of harm", "HAZARD = a software defect; HAZARDOUS SITUATION = a defect that reaches a released product", "HAZARD = the potential source of harm; HAZARDOUS SITUATION = the circumstances where a person is exposed to that hazard", "HAZARD and HAZARDOUS SITUATION are defined as synonymous in Amendment 1"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Amendment 1 clarified: a HAZARD is a potential source of harm (e.g., incorrect dose calculation), while a HAZARDOUS SITUATION is the circumstance in which a person is exposed to that hazard (e.g., patient receives an incorrect dose). Software failure modes must be linked to hazardous situations, not just to abstract hazards.', 2)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000003', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'IEC 62304 §5.3 requires SOUP to be documented in the architectural design. Which set of information is required as a minimum?', '["The SOUP''s complete source code and build scripts", "Title, manufacturer, version identifier, intended use, functional requirements it must meet, and its required operating environment", "The SOUP''s CE marking certificate or FDA 510(k) clearance number", "The SOUP''s full validation test history and a list of all known anomalies"]'::jsonb, 1, '§5.3 requires SOUP to be identified by: name/title, manufacturer, version or revision identifier, intended use within the system, the functional and performance requirements it must meet, and the hardware/software environment it requires. This information is needed to evaluate SOUP as a configuration item and to assess whether its known anomalies are relevant.', 3)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000004', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'A configuration management record identifies a SOUP component as "latest stable release." Does this satisfy IEC 62304 §8?', '["Yes, if the SOUP vendor provides regular security updates", "Yes, for Class A and B software only", "No \u2014 SOUP must be identified by an exact version or revision identifier", "No \u2014 SOUP must not be used unless the full source code is available for review"]'::jsonb, 2, '§8 requires all SOUP items to be under configuration management with an exact version or revision identifier recorded. "Latest" or "current" is not acceptable because it prevents the manufacturer from reproducing the exact configuration used in any released product — a requirement that may need to be met years later during a regulatory investigation.', 4)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000005', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'After release, the manufacturer discovers a known anomaly in a SOUP component. What does IEC 62304 §7 require?', '["Immediately withdraw the product from the market pending investigation", "Evaluate whether the anomaly could contribute to a hazardous situation in the intended use environment and document the assessment with a conclusion", "Notify the SOUP vendor and await a patch before taking any further action", "Issue a corrective software update within 30 days of discovery"]'::jsonb, 1, '§7 requires that for each known anomaly in a SOUP item, the manufacturer assesses whether it could contribute to a hazardous situation in the intended use environment and documents the conclusion. Market withdrawal is only required if the risk assessment determines that the risk is unacceptable and cannot be mitigated otherwise.', 5)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000006', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'A Class C software item implements a risk control measure identified in the ISO 14971 risk management file. Which IEC 62304 clause governs the requirement to verify its effectiveness?', '["Clause 5.7 \u2014 Software System Testing", "Clause 5.8 \u2014 Software Release", "Clause 7 \u2014 Software Risk Management", "Clause 9 \u2014 Problem Resolution"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Clause 7 requires that software items implementing risk control measures are verified as effective. The verification evidence must feed into the ISO 14971 risk management file to demonstrate that the control measure functions as intended. System testing (§5.7) provides the test evidence, but the requirement to verify effectiveness is a §7 obligation.', 6)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000007', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'Under §5.8, under what condition may a manufacturer release software that has unresolved known anomalies?', '["Never \u2014 all anomalies must be resolved before release is permitted", "Only for Class A software", "When every known residual anomaly has been documented and evaluated to confirm it does not contribute to an unacceptable risk", "Only when the anomalies are user interface issues with no functional impact"]'::jsonb, 2, '§5.8 does not require zero open anomalies at release. §5.8.2 requires all known residual anomalies to be documented, for every safety class. §5.8.3 then requires the manufacturer to ensure those anomalies have been evaluated to confirm they do not contribute to an unacceptable risk, for Class B and C. Note what the standard does not say: IEC 62304 does not itself prescribe who authorises the release. That sits with the manufacturer''s quality management system under ISO 13485.', 7)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000008', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'During a §5.5 unit verification activity for Class C software, a defect is found and silently fixed by the developer without logging a problem report. Is this acceptable under IEC 62304?', '["Yes, if the fix is verified and the unit re-tested successfully", "Yes, if the defect was found before the unit was formally baselined", "No \u2014 all anomalies found during verification must be documented through the Clause 9 problem resolution process", "No \u2014 but only if the defect affected a safety-related software item"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Clause 9 requires all problems to be logged regardless of when they are found. Silent fixes — even those re-verified successfully — bypass the required safety impact assessment and root cause analysis. Undocumented fixes are one of the most common critical findings in notified body audits of Class C software.', 8)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000009', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'What specific addition did Amendment 1 make to the requirements of §5.1 Software Development Planning?', '["It added a requirement to specify the waterfall lifecycle model as the default", "It removed the requirement to reference ISO 13485 in the plan", "It added an explicit requirement to address cybersecurity in the software development plan", "It added a requirement to produce a separate test plan for each software item"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Amendment 1 added cybersecurity as a topic that must be explicitly addressed in the software development plan, including how security requirements are identified, allocated to software items, implemented, and verified. The original 2006 standard had no explicit cybersecurity planning requirement.', 9)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000010', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'A software engineer proposes using a static analysis tool to extract comments from completed code and format them as the "detailed design" documentation for Class C. What is the correct assessment?', '["Acceptable, provided the static analysis tool is listed in the software development plan", "Acceptable for Class B but not Class C", "Not acceptable \u2014 detailed design must describe intended behaviour before implementation, not document what was built after the fact", "Acceptable if the output is reviewed and approved by a second engineer"]'::jsonb, 2, '§5.4.2 requires a design documented in enough detail to allow correct implementation of each software unit — it is the basis for implementation, not a retrospective description of it. §5.4.4 then requires the detailed design to be verified as implementing the software architecture and as free from contradiction with it, a check that is meaningless if the design was generated from the finished code. Extracting documentation from existing code reverses the required sequence and demonstrates no planned design intent.', 10)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000011', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'Under §6, a change request is received to add a new clinical feature to released Class C software. Which development activities are required?', '["The maintenance process only \u2014 new features are categorised as maintenance activities", "A brief impact assessment followed by direct implementation and regression testing", "The full \u00a75 development activities appropriate for the safety class of the affected software items, including requirements, design, testing, and risk management", "The change must be rejected \u2014 new features require a new regulatory submission before implementation"]'::jsonb, 2, '§6 requires that changes to released software that affect safety-related software items re-apply the relevant §5 development activities at the depth appropriate for the safety class. Adding new features is not a pure maintenance activity — it requires requirements analysis, design, risk management, and testing to be applied to the new and affected software items.', 11)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000012', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'Which of the following correctly defines "legacy software" as introduced in §4.4 (Amendment 1)?', '["Software that was developed more than 10 years before the current review", "Software legally placed on the market and still marketed, but without sufficient objective evidence that it was developed in compliance with the current version of the standard", "Software that was developed for a previous device version and reused without modification", "Software that has not been validated for the current intended use of the device"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Definition 3.36, added by Amendment 1, defines legacy software as medical device software legally placed on the market and still marketed today, but for which there is insufficient objective evidence that it was developed in compliance with the current version of the standard. The test is missing evidence of compliance — not the software''s age, and not merely that it predates the standard. §4.4 then offers a route to compliance: risk management activities, a gap analysis of available deliverables against §5.2, §5.3, §5.7 and Clause 7, a plan to close the gaps with software system test records as the minimum deliverable, and a documented rationale for continued use — instead of full retrospective development documentation.', 12)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000013', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'Under §9, a problem is investigated and determined not to be a software defect. What does IEC 62304 require?', '["Nothing \u2014 only confirmed defects need to be formally recorded", "Record the problem and the rationale for the \"not a defect\" conclusion", "Record it only if found in a safety-related software item", "Escalate to the risk management team for independent review"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Clause 9 requires all problems to be logged, including those ultimately determined not to be defects. The record must include the rationale for closure. Undocumented investigations — even for non-defects — are a common critical finding during regulatory audits because they leave gaps in the objective evidence trail.', 13)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, course_version_id, level, question, options, correct_index, explanation, sort_order)
values ('33333333-3333-3333-3333-200000000014', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222', 'advanced', 'A bidirectional traceability matrix is required under IEC 62304. What must it trace in both directions?', '["Source code commits to developer names, and developer names to their qualifications", "Software requirements to system requirements, and software requirements to test cases", "Risk control measures to test cases only", "Software items to their assigned safety class, and safety classes to the risk management file"]'::jsonb, 1, '§5.2 and §5.7 together require bidirectional traceability: each software requirement must trace up to a system requirement (ensuring nothing is implemented without a system-level justification) and down to a test case (ensuring everything required is tested). Gaps in either direction are a common finding in technical file reviews.', 14)
on conflict (id) do update set question = excluded.question, options = excluded.options, correct_index = excluded.correct_index, explanation = excluded.explanation, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;
